          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ചിത്രകാരൻ — citrakāran — \"a painter\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ആ ചിത്രകാരന്റെ ചിത്രങ്ങൾ പ്രദർശനത്തിൽ ഉണ്ടായിരുന്നു. ā citrakāranṟe citraṅṅaḷ pradarśanattil uṇṭāyirunnu. That painter's pictures were in the exhibition."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A woman painter is ചിത്രകാരി."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ചിത്രകാരൻ (citrakāran) is borrowed from Sanskrit citrakāra, \"a painter\" (CDIAL 4807), citra, \"a picture\", and kāra, \"a maker\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
